{"path":"numeric/random/uniform_random_bit_generator","title":"std::uniform_random_bit_generator","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>uniform_random_bit_generator","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/random/uniform_random_bit_generator","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The concept uniform_random_bit_generator<G> specifies that G is the type of a uniform random bit generator, that is, objects of type G is a function object returning unsigned integer values such that each value in the range of possible…","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/random\">&lt;random&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> G <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept uniform_random_bit_generator <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/invocable\"><span class=\"kw2976\">std::<span class=\"me2\">invocable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>G<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/unsigned_integral\"><span class=\"kw2958\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unsigned_integral</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/result_of\"><span class=\"kw3239\">std::<span class=\"me2\">invoke_result_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>G<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <span class=\"br0\">{</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"br0\">{</span> G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2951\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/result_of\"><span class=\"kw3239\">std::<span class=\"me2\">invoke_result_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>G<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"br0\">{</span> G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2951\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/result_of\"><span class=\"kw3239\">std::<span class=\"me2\">invoke_result_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>G<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integral_constant\"><span class=\"kw653\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bool_constant</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The concept <code>uniform_random_bit_generator&lt;G&gt;</code> specifies that <code>G</code> is the type of a uniform random bit generator, that is, objects of type <code>G</code> is a function object returning unsigned integer values such that each value in the range of possible results has (ideally) equal probability of being returned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Semantic_requirements\">Semantic requirements</h3>\n<p><code>uniform_random_bit_generator&lt;G&gt;</code> is modeled only if, given any object <code>g</code> of type <code>G</code>:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code>g()</code> is in the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>]</code></span>,\n</li><li> <code>g()</code> has amortized constant complexity.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>In order to satisfy the requirement <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integral_constant\"><span class=\"kw653\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bool_constant</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code>, both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">G<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> must be constant expressions, and the result of the comparison must be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>.\n</p>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Semantic requirements","id":"Semantic_requirements"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/random","title":"Pseudo-random number generation"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::uniform_random_bit_generator","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. The concept uniform_random_bit_generator<G> specifies that G is the type of a uniform random bit generator, that is…"},{"label":"Semantic requirements","note":"uniform_random_bit_generator<G> is modeled only if, given any object g of type G:"},{"label":"Notes","note":"In order to satisfy the requirement std::bool_constant<(G::min() < G::max())>::value, both G::min() and G::max() must be constant expressions, and the result…"}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":132,"codeBlockCount":0}
